Package: tarpolyglot
Type: Package
Title: Run 'Python', 'Julia', 'Rust', and 'C++' Inside 'targets' Pipeline Steps
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      given = "Pierre",
      family = "Solomon",
      email = "pierre.solomon@laposte.net",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7187-2664")
    )
  )
Description: Adds target constructors that make it easy to use 'Python', 'Julia',
    'Rust', and 'C++' inside a 'targets' pipeline using 'reticulate', 'JuliaCall',
    'rextendr', and 'Rcpp'. Provides tar_target_py(), tar_target_jl(),
    tar_target_rs(), and tar_target_cpp() (with matching _raw() variants), each
    mirroring 'targets' tar_target() and tar_target_raw() functions. 'Python'
    and 'Julia' steps run a script via a live interpreter with optional R pre-
    and post-scripts; 'Rust' and 'C++' steps compile functions and call them 
    from an R post-script. Results are then returned either as converted R
    objects or as files written to disk (format = "file"). Dynamic branching,
    environment/version selection, a 'crew' controller for isolation, and the
    full set of tar_target_raw() arguments are supported.
